        "field_path": [
          "study_summary_A",
          "research_scope"
        ],
        "value": "The review focuses on the role of the gut microbiome in modulating responses to immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) targeting PD-1/PD-L1 and CTLA-4 in patients with advanced solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, GI cancers). It covers preclinical evidence from mouse models, observational human data linking microbiota composition to clinical outcomes and adverse events, potential biological mechanisms, and early-phase clinical trials of microbiome-based interventions.",
