onse, which provides biological rationale for ongoing trials. For example, Fusobacterium nucleatum (Fn) is described as promoting immune evasion via Fap2-TIGIT binding and chemotherapy resistance, while Peptostreptococcus anaerobius (Pa) is linked to anti–PD-1 resistance via MDSC activation. Conversely, beneficial bacteria like Bifidobacterium are noted in preclinical models to enhance antitumor efficacy of PD-1 blockade. The authors also discuss confounding factors in microbiome research (e.g., stool transit time, BMI) that complicate biomarker and intervention standardization, relevant for designing future rigorous trials.\", \"The review details methodological heterogeneity across the included studies, such as variations in sequencing regions (V3-V4, V4, V4-V5), sample collection times, and cancer types, which complicates direct comparison. It also notes that only two studies examined gastrointestinal toxicity (colitis), finding low Bacteroidetes abundance associated with higher risk. The authors mention that while FMT response rates in these small studies are comparable to RCTs for Clostridioides difficile infection, the cancer FMT studies themselves are described as 'breakthrough clinical studies' rather than large-scale Phase III trials. The review excludes animal models to focus on clinical applicability but acknowledges that most included studies are observational (retrospective or prospective cohorts) rather than randomized interventions.\"]\n\n现有材料未提供已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤中的疗效。相反，多项研究明确指出该领域仍处于早期阶段：MITRIC 试验是一项单臂 IIa 期篮子试验，结果显示在 ICI 难治性晚期癌症患者中 FMT 无客观缓解（ORR 0%），仅个别患者获得临床获益；TACITO 试验虽为随机双盲安慰剂对照试验，但仅为 IIa 期，且主要终点（12个月无进展生存率）未达到统计学显著差异（70% vs 41%, P=0.053），尽管次要终点中位 PFS 有显著改善（24.0 vs 9.0 个月, P=0.035）。此外，一项涵盖 10 项研究（164 名患者）的系统综述与荟萃分析指出，目前证据主要来自早期 Phase I/II 试验和小样本 RCT，作者明确强调“缺乏大型随机对照试验”，并呼吁进行大规模、多中心的 III 期 RCT 以确认疗效和优化方案。因此，截至这些来源的时间点，尚无完成的 III 期 RCT 确证其疗效，这一证据缺口被反复提及为当前研究的局限性及未来方向。\n\n现有材料未提供已完成的大型随机对照 III 期临床试验证实微生物干预（如 FMT）在 ICI 治疗实体瘤